            "Unresolved": [
              "UNRESOLVED (p.409-414): first / last A101 line from the deck ends - the plans give the counts and the maximum spacings (1924 @ 6\u0022 top, 2199 @ 5 1/4\u0022 bottom) but no distance of the first line from the deck end. Lines equally spaced at the maximum spacing, centred between the deck ends along the left edge.",
              "UNRESOLVED (p.409, p.414): top #4 B104 / B105 / B106 in the end spans 30 and 35 - the plans give the bar lengths and only MINIMUM laps (2\u0027-2\u0022), not the bar positions. Reading: laid from the deck end (3\u0022 cover) with 2\u0027-2\u0022 laps between the #4 bars, the rest is the lap onto the #6 B102 (lap onto the #6 B102: span 30 53.54-53.54 in, span 35 24.16-24.16 in).",
              "CONFLICT (p.409 / p.414): the printed #4 bar lengths with 2\u0027-2\u0022 minimum #4 laps and a 3\u0022 end cover leave 24.16 in. of lap onto the #6 B102, less than the 2\u0027-2\u0022 minimum (#4 to #6) - modeled as read, not adjusted.",
              "UNRESOLVED (p.448 / p.451): parapet bars B8 / B9 (6 bars) and B10 / B11 (2 bars) in the last section at bent 35 - the plan lists 6 \u002B 2 bars of two lengths per side but does not show which of the 8 positions take the shorter B10 / B11. Schedule only at the bill counts and lengths.",
              "UNRESOLVED (p.405): diaphragm bars E301-E304 in the sloped ends - they are drawn as sloped lines inside the wedge (\u00273\u0022 CLR. MIN.\u0027 to the face only); their four lengths (5\u0027-9\u0022 to 8\u0027-2\u0022) do not tell which line each one is on or where it starts. Schedule only.",
              "UNRESOLVED (p.407 / p.408): G302 (modular joint support boxes) and G301 (Transflex blockout) - G302 sits \u0027@ ea. support box\u0027 of the supplier-designed modular joint (box positions not in the plans); G301 \u00274-#5G301 @ 10\u0022 CTS. (TYP. EA. GIRDER)\u0027 has no dimension to the girder or to the blockout. Schedule only.",
              "UNRESOLVED (p.405-408): K301, K303-K307, K309 / K310, S301-S304, S307-S311, U308, U310 / U311 - drawn in Sections K-K, L-L, M-M, N-N and the typical sections, but the runs (K305 / K306 / K307 two-bar runs through the 1 1/2\u0022 web holes: 32 K307 per bent diaphragm do not resolve into the drawn 16), the S309 tie pattern (82 per bay) and the end diaphragm stirrup chains are not dimensioned enough to place without guessing. Schedule only at the bill counts and lengths.",
              "UNRESOLVED (p.445): access opening bars H1-H6 - H4 / H6 are mechanically coupled to the H7 outside the opening and H1 / H2 / H3 / H5 are drawn around it, but only H7 has a length and a group inside the opening that fixes it. Schedule only; the openings are temporary (filled with MAP concrete), no hole is cut in the deck."
            ]
          },
